From 7ce30bdffd3b3d51884b29145f3461f1bea37d87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HiGarfield <HiGarfield@126.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:45:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] smbd: add SMB2.1 protocol support

Implement the SMB2.1 dialect (2.002 / 0x0210) on top of the existing
SMB2.0.2 code path:

* Negotiate: advertise SMB2.1 in the dialect table, report the
  negotiated dialect and enable multi-credit (large MTU) when the
  dialect is >= 0x0210.
* Credit accounting: charge and grant credits across read, write,
  create, getinfo, setinfo, find and notify.
* IOCTL FSCTL_VALIDATE_NEGOTIATE_INFO validation of the client
  negotiate request.
* Session setup channel binding (BINDING vs dedicated) for
  multi-channel capable clients.
* Loadparm: add the SMB2_21 enum value, raise the server max protocol
  defaults, and add the "smb2 durable handles" parameter.
* Raise the default read/write/transact sizes to 1MB and update the
  protocol enum and constants accordingly.

All dialect-gated features are gated on a >= 0x0210 comparison so the
SMB2.0.2 behaviour is preserved for older clients.
